# ArchiMate AI Studio — core conventions

## Architecture source of truth

In-repo: `docs/architecture/` (overview, technology, modules, ADRs, cybersecurity, delivery).

## Solution layout

- `src/ArchiMateAiStudio.Domain` — patches, proposals, ports
- `src/ArchiMateAiStudio.Archimate` — XSD, parser, validator, patch applicator
- `src/ArchiMateAiStudio.Application` — use cases (MediatR later)
- `src/ArchiMateAiStudio.Infrastructure` — RunPod, EF, R2, Redis adapters
- `src/ArchiMateAiStudio.Api` — REST `/api/v1`
- `tests/ArchiMateAiStudio.Archimate.Tests` — xUnit unit + API smoke

## Non-negotiables

1. **`.archimate` XML is canonical** — AI changes go through `ModelPatch` + approved `ChangeProposal`
2. **Archi-compatible IDs** — `id-` + 32 lowercase hex via `ArchiMateIdGenerator`
3. **RunPod only via `ILlmChatClient`** — stub in CI; no direct HTTP from controllers
4. **ArchiSurance 3.2** — official Open Group reference model (Y194M) for round-trip tests; not a typo

## Subagents (repo-local)

| Agent | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `/project-architect` | Solution architecture in `docs/architecture/` |
| `/enterprise-architect` | EA requirements, viewpoints, traceability |
| `/cybersecurity-design` | SEC-* requirements, RunPod/RAG security |
| `/cicd-release` | GitHub Actions, deploy, ArchiSurance CI job |
| `/tdd` | Test-first C# implementation |
| `/architecture-compliance` | Pre-release alignment check |

## Phases

0 — Model CRUD + XSD | 1 — RunPod patch loop | 2 — Ingestion + RAG | 3 — Agents + views
